    "created_at": "2025-11-21T13:43:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-21T13:43:11Z",
    "body": "> I followed blame back to https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=931884#c10 (starting at [6bdba31](https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/6bdba31102d6aea442b215fe485093c0ad322425)) which suggests to me that obtaining an `Origin` from `Location` or `WorkerLocation` is not something we should offer by default. You can still do it by passing `location.href`, if you really know what you're doing, but in general those objects don't really hold the authority and so we shouldn't encourage that.\r\n\r\nI understand your point, but it seems [unlikely](https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/1827) we're going to be able to get rid of `location.origin` given its usage, it would be slightly odd for this to be the only interface with an `origin` property that `Origin.from()` wouldn't support. I think I'd suggest erring on the side of consistency, but I don't hold that opinion too strongly.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3563086422/reactions",
